  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=12.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have  a block lower triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ r & 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & q & 5 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
